    {
      "repository": "vorssaint/vorssaint-utils",
      "url": "https://github.com/vorssaint/vorssaint-utils",
      "trending_rank": 14,
      "description": "Vorssaint is a ==free macOS menu bar toolkit== that bundles utilities Mac users often buy separately: a per-app volume mixer, a system monitor with fan control, an app switcher and window snapping, Dock previews, clipboard history, text snippets, a file shelf, screen capture and recording, an uninstaller and a Homebrew manager. You install only the features you want; unused ones stop loading.",
      "why_interesting": "First time on our list, and a break from the AI tooling that fills most of the listing. It replaces ==a dozen small paid utilities with one open-source app==, and its privacy notes list every network connection it can make (update checks, an on-demand speed test, optional lyrics lookup, temporary share links, feedback) and state that it collects no usage statistics or crash reports. Releases are signed and notarized, and it installs with Homebrew.",
      "caveat": "==Apple Silicon Macs on macOS 14 or newer only==. Many features need Accessibility, Screen Recording or Microphone permission, which gives one app broad control of your Mac; each permission is optional. Fan Control is beta. Temporary screenshot and recording links upload to Vorssaint's service, and anyone with a link can view and save the file until it expires. Licensed GPL-3.0. We did not install or run it, so the privacy statements are the maintainers' own.",
      "category": "Desktop utilities / macOS",
      "language": "Swift",
      "license": "GPL-3.0",
      "stars_total": 32056,
