    {
      "repository": "bregman-arie/devops-exercises",
      "url": "https://github.com/bregman-arie/devops-exercises",
      "trending_rank": 13,
      "description": "A large, ==free bank of DevOps and SRE questions and exercises==, with answers folded under each question. It covers Linux, networking, Git, Docker, Kubernetes, Terraform, Ansible, AWS, Azure, GCP, Prometheus, databases, Python and more; the README counts 2,624 questions and exercises. It is plain Markdown, so there is nothing to install.",
      "why_interesting": "First time on our list, and the only infrastructure-learning project on today's list. It is a long-running community resource, created in 2019, that is useful for ==self-testing across the whole operations stack== rather than one tool, and the hands-on exercises go beyond trivia questions.",
      "caveat": "The last commit is from 27 December 2025, so ==some answers may lag current tool versions==, and community-written answers are not reviewed like a textbook. The README warns that most questions do not represent real interviews. GitHub detects no licence: the LICENSE file is Creative Commons legal text that allows ==non-commercial sharing without adaptations==, so it cannot be reworked into a paid course.",
      "category": "Learning / DevOps and SRE",
